body:
The `/api/auth/profile` endpoint was called unconditionally on every app load, generating 401 errors and unnecessary server logs when users were unauthenticated.

## Changes

**Frontend authentication flow**
- Added localStorage flag `isAuthenticated` to gate profile checks on initial app load
- Modified `checkAuth()` to accept optional skip parameter for initial load vs explicit refresh scenarios
- Flag lifecycle: set on login/signup, cleared on logout/auth failures, restored on successful profile checks

**Code cleanup**
- Removed 198 lines of commented code across 6 files (old Stripe implementation, unused store, debug comments)

## Example

Before:
```javascript
// App.jsx - unconditional call
useEffect(() => {
  checkAuth();  // Always hits API
}, [checkAuth]);
```

After:
```javascript
// App.jsx - conditional based on prior auth state
useEffect(() => {
  checkAuth(true);  // Skips if localStorage flag absent
}, [checkAuth]);

// useUserStore.js
checkAuth: async (skipIfUnauthenticated = false) => {
  set({ checkingAuth: true });

  if (skipIfUnauthenticated && !localStorage.getItem("isAuthenticated")) {
    set({ checkingAuth: false, user: null });
    return;
  }

  // Proceed with API call...
}
```

The backend authentication middleware remains unchanged; this is purely a client-side optimization to prevent unnecessary requests.

